{"event_type":"review","id":"65a1963f51136dd4099693fd534906526f9861ffebc0c43d6b924d67bfe9ee25","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T19:48:47Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f19320dd60d8b42ff876cafa102ec509c72cc722954120f912daf72955558bf1","sha256":"f19320dd60d8b42ff876cafa102ec509c72cc722954120f912daf72955558bf1"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/bb32ce7bbf0baa6e2f9e77e3b11b4352c594dc745134a55e705b385f5f738839","sha256":"bb32ce7bbf0baa6e2f9e77e3b11b4352c594dc745134a55e705b385f5f738839"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3db188cb4b917dbf3fb762c917a57f8a250b4bec188bd0d426f02a0aab074bf5","sha256":"3db188cb4b917dbf3fb762c917a57f8a250b4bec188bd0d426f02a0aab074bf5"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c8046cc816a30defcd8da667b5ef9eb2b921cdc5089c3d003a9985dd5c7c0321","sha256":"c8046cc816a30defcd8da667b5ef9eb2b921cdc5089c3d003a9985dd5c7c0321"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/656f082243bfd07164b8f4d8a42cd775ba2ed51582a384a616ae75500b42aab8","sha256":"656f082243bfd07164b8f4d8a42cd775ba2ed51582a384a616ae75500b42aab8"}],"attempt_id":"390840043025ec593c4048ce3eb1967c516cf7224a83a702b2124347c1b4af04:0:1","base":"fb63ec75bfb016c8283b73e88ba46b46c66d4d34","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"90f669aec8fade830010bc798b7d8961b4050bd3","body":"**`login:authorType` matching is case-sensitive and not documented as such.**\n\nGitHub logins are case-insensitive. The checks `entry === authorLogin` and `authorLogin === config.automationLogin` do exact-string comparison. A `trustedAuthors` entry with different casing fails closed, which is safe. An `excludedLogins` entry with different casing fails open. The excluded user then passes if `trustedAuthors` also lists them in another casing.\n\nNormalise with `toLowerCase()` on both sides of the exclusion and automation checks.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  if (authorLogin === config.automationLogin || config.excludedLogins?.includes(authorLogin))\n-    return false;\n+  const login = authorLogin.toLowerCase();\n+  if (\n+    login === config.automationLogin?.toLowerCase() ||\n+    config.excludedLogins?.some((excluded) => excluded.toLowerCase() === login)\n+  )\n+    return false;\n```\n</details>","id":"fa64790e99352dc8e658a249f7fe85477fd77ee9a549daf42e3c1102151b33ab","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/classifyThreads.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"`login:authorType` matching is case-sensitive and not documented as such."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"cd78ee2cd8b425ec0bb99407b53d4ec02d2cbbea","body":"**`ESCAPED_KEY_RE` backtracks quadratically on long lines of escapes.**\n\nThe pattern `\"(?:[^\"\\\\]|\\\\.)*\\\\(?:[^\"\\\\]|\\\\.)*\"` has two adjacent star groups that both accept `\\\\.`. A single escape can match either the first group or the middle `\\\\`. Take a line such as `{\"` followed by many `\\n` escapes, with no closing quote. The engine tries every split point and rescans the tail each time. Cost is O(n²) per start position.\n\n`carriesMalformedStringField` (Line 310) and `reconstructLifecycle` run this regex on every `-`, `+` and context line of the diff. The diff content is PR-author controlled. A crafted baseline line of a few hundred KB can stall `checkDiffMonotonicity`. The other key and value regexes in this file use a single star group and stay linear.\n\nPut the escape in the pattern once, after an escape-free prefix. The match semantics are unchanged: the key must contain at least one escape.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-const ESCAPED_KEY_RE = /(?:^|[,{])\\s*\"(?:[^\"\\\\]|\\\\.)*\\\\(?:[^\"\\\\]|\\\\.)*\"\\s*:/;\n+const ESCAPED_KEY_RE = /(?:^|[,{])\\s*\"[^\"\\\\]*\\\\.(?:[^\"\\\\]|\\\\.)*\"\\s*:/;\n```\n</details>\n\nThe result stays fail-closed, because a hang times out the gate. The cost is a stalled CI job, not a bypass.","id":"d6cb06840992760c54e25a2e18ee8e7b13375dce93c8ec11ffdf5175a2210d34","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/ratchet/monotonicGuard.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"`ESCAPEDKEYRE` backtracks quadratically on long lines of escapes."}],"head":"68de9fbeaa4d5ae1137f002861afbe3f686dfd1c","head_tree":"067d49da10942551a3c39da201ad1d79467f9afa","input_scope":[{"blob":"060cb1c77e09f02a26ab5dbab39db956db204b2e","intervals":[[58,59],[270,270],[293,294],[301,302],[326,327],[351,352],[387,388],[489,495],[501,503]],"path":"src/ops/ratchet/captureBaseline.ts"},{"blob":"cd78ee2cd8b425ec0bb99407b53d4ec02d2cbbea","intervals":[[16,19],[22,43],[113,118],[127,134],[179,182],[241,242],[257,257],[309,311],[356,356],[437,438],[440,441],[446,446],[482,485],[487,488],[513,516],[523,526],[528,529],[552,559],[565,568],[570,571],[582,695],[700,703],[713,716],[720,734],[736,736],[755,762],[764,767],[770,773],[791,791],[814,820]],"path":"src/ops/ratchet/monotonicGuard.ts"},{"blob":"90f669aec8fade830010bc798b7d8961b4050bd3","intervals":[[97,97],[211,236],[275,279],[287,291],[299,303],[333,333],[337,351],[381,381],[401,401],[405,409],[471,475],[482,482],[496,500],[502,502],[515,515],[553,554],[556,556],[558,558]],"path":"src/ops/review/classifyThreads.ts"},{"blob":"f723143687eafe97c170bd5d589ef8f2d8b72caa","intervals":[[6,6],[38,39],[62,69],[103,110],[113,114],[170,171],[284,286],[294,297],[307,310],[328,328],[367,369],[376,376],[443,443],[462,469],[472,474],[479,495],[506,506],[508,508],[516,545],[560,560],[572,575],[591,591],[603,610]],"path":"src/ops/review/replyAndResolve.ts"}],"job_id":"390840043025ec593c4048ce3eb1967c516cf7224a83a702b2124347c1b4af04:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"eed945d3ef5e585878f332761cb5bc5e1139ec11","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","